{
  "id": "DrugBank_DB00324 - MONDO_17210",
  "verbalization": "Fluorometholone, a corticosteroid, is implicated in the pathogenesis of Infectious Anterior Uveitis through a mechanism involving Medrysone, a known inducer of this condition. The evidence suggests that Fluorometholone, through its indication for Iritis and Uveitis, leads to the use of Medrysone, which in turn is associated with Infectious Anterior Uveitis. This creates a chain of indications that links Fluorometholone to the disease through Medrysone, highlighting a potential role of corticosteroids in the development of this condition. The overlapping pathways indicate that Fluorometholone may contribute to the progression of Infectious Anterior Uveitis via a shared pathway involving Medrysone, suggesting a possible pharmacological relationship that warrants further investigation.",
